Time::HiRes: take the win32 branch when the TARGET is Windows.

Makefile.PL keys its win32 configuration on $^O, which is the build host's
(linux) under perl-cross, so it ran the probe path instead: no
TIME_HIRES_CLOCK_GETTIME/GETRES, and clock_gettime/clock_getres died with
"unimplemented in this platform". The win32 branch selects HiRes.xs's own
QueryPerformanceCounter implementations, as on a native Windows build.

--- a/dist/Time-HiRes/Makefile.PL
+++ b/dist/Time-HiRes/Makefile.PL
@@ -1042,7 +1042,7 @@
     } else {
         print "Configuring Time::HiRes...\n";
         1 while unlink("define");
-        if ($^O =~ /Win32/i) {
+        if ($^O =~ /Win32/i || $Config{osname} =~ /Win32/i) {
             DEFINE('SELECT_IS_BROKEN');
             # we provide our own implementations of those functions on win32
             DEFINE('TIME_HIRES_CLOCK_GETTIME');
